I stand at the bus stop with the yellow flowers.
There are many people who are waiting.
I look at the screen to see the timetable.
The bus is supposed to be here in five minutes.
I think that the Friday traffic is often very slow.
But the streets look completely empty today.
So I think that the bus will probably arrive on time.
An older man stands next to me.
He looks at his watch and sighs.
"Do you know if the bus is late?" he asks me.
I check my phone again.
"No, I don't think so," I answer.
"I actually also intend to take the same bus."
"I think that it is actually just around the corner."
He smiles at me and nods.
Suddenly we see the big yellow bus down the street.
It drives quickly towards us.
"You were right," the man says happily.
We step onto the bus together.
I will definitely be at Eva's place on time.
I am excited to see her apartment.
